<h2>Spartanburg claim questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>A tree from my neighbor’s yard fell on my house. Whose insurance pays?</summary><div class="a"><p>In most cases your own homeowners policy responds to damage to your house, regardless of where the tree stood. Questions about the neighbor’s responsibility are legal ones for a South Carolina attorney.</p></div></details><details><summary>My detached garage was crushed. Is that part of the dwelling claim?</summary><div class="a"><p>Usually it falls under other structures coverage, which has its own limit. We itemize it separately so it is not lost inside the main dwelling estimate.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can you match materials on an old mill house?</summary><div class="a"><p>We price the materials and methods needed to restore the home to its pre-loss condition, including older lumber sizes and siding profiles, and explain the cost basis to the other side.</p></div></details></div>
